Multiplayer:
    User Interface:
        ☐ Design a graphical interface for the game.
        ☐ Add a mini-map showing the player's position and the complete map.
        ☐ Implement wall and player graphics (similar to Maze Wars).
        ☐ Display real-time frame rate (FPS) on screen.
    Architecture:
        Client-Server:
            ☐ Implement client-server architecture.
            ☐ Enable client and server to run on the same machine.
            ☐ Allow multiple clients to connect from different machines.
            ☐ Use the UDP protocol for communication between clients and server.

        Server:
            ☐ Create a server capable of handling at least 10 simultaneous connections.
            ☐ Implement logic to manage connections and communication between clients.
        Client:
            ☐ On initialization, request the following information:
            ☐ The server's IP address.
            ☐ A user name to identify the player.
            ☐ Start the game with a graphical interface after initialization.
        Gameplay:
            ☐ Implement 3 game levels with increasing difficulty.
            ☐ Level 1: Simple maze.
            ☐ Level 2: Intermediate maze with more dead ends.
            ☐ Level 3: Complex maze with many traps.
            ☐ Ensure that the game maintains a refresh rate of over 50 FPS.
    Bonus Features: 
        ☐ Create a level editor to allow players to design their own mazes.
        ☐ Add an algorithm to automatically generate new mazes.
        ☐ Implement players controlled by Artificial Intelligence (AI).
        ☐ Improve initialization:
        ☐ Add a graphical interface for initial configuration.
        ☐ Save server history with an alias to simplify reconnections.
    Testing and performance:
        ☐ Test gameplay to guarantee fluidity above 50 FPS.
        ☐ Test connectivity between client and server via UDP.
        ☐ Validate that the server accepts and manages at least 10 simultaneous connections.
